<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/16th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peace of Passau</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1552">1552</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Peace of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/passau">Passau</a> was an agreement of August 1552 between King Ferdinand I, acting for Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-v-holy-roman-emperor">Charles V</a>, and the Protestant princes led by Maurice of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony">Saxony</a>, who had risen against the emperor in the Princes' Revolt. It released the captive Landgrave Philip of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a> and granted Lutherans freedom of worship until a diet could settle the religious question, which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-augsburg">Peace of Augsburg</a> did in 1555.</p></div>
